a standoff in the belgian capital on the  sidelines of a kovid 19 protest  police used water cannon against a group  of protesters  some of whom appeared to throw fireworks  several hundred people marched through  the streets two days after the  government tightened restrictions for  the third week in a row  some carried signs critical of vaccines  which have proved to be highly effective  against the coronavirus  others were worried about belgium making  it compulsory for health workers to be  vaccinated something that's coming in on  the 1st of january  i don't agree with mandatory vaccination  for nurses  i think every person has the choice to  take a vaccine  that's his own choice  and that's freedom in my opinion  health workers will have three months to  get their shots they can work during  that time if they can show they've  already had kovid 19 or provide negative  tests hospital admissions have risen by  4 week on week but the government says  40 of belgium's intensive care beds are  currently filled by covid19 patients and  that's having an impact on things like  cancer treatments  kindergartens and primary schools will  now close a week early for christmas and  pupils aged six or over have to wear  face masks  indoor venues such as cinemas will be  limited to 200 people from monday  nightclubs have already been closed and  bars and restaurants have to shut at 11  pm for three weeks nadeem baba al  jazeera
 

